; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR MOONBASE  -  a text adventure   (VM1 @ $4000, SETSIZE 3)
; ==========================================================================
; A moonquake has wrecked Moonbase Tycho. The crew got away without you, the
; air is running out, and the last lander is out on the crater floor. Get to
; it and get it off the ground.
;
; Type commands of one or two words: N, S, E, W, UP, DOWN, IN, OUT, LOOK,
; INVENTORY (I), TAKE WRENCH, DROP, EXAMINE LOCKER, OPEN, READ, WEAR, USE,
; TURN ON FLASHLIGHT, PUSH, TYPE, HELP, QUIT. Any case. Only the first four
; letters of a word count. Every move uses air.
;
; 10 rooms, 16 objects (5 to carry), 134 words. The parser is native 1802 at
; $4C00 (Firmware-Math/adventure_native.asm, 288 bytes, run with RUNMC after
; each line); the game is the STELLAR program below. Edit the world - rooms,
; exits, objects, words, messages - in Firmware-Math/build_adventure.py.
;
; MEMORY. SETSIZE 3 takes $4000-$6FFF, so load it with no program in the $5000
; or $6000 blocks. Messages $5200-$6EFF, variables and the typed line $6F00-$6FFF.
; Everything the game changes is reset at the start of each game, so it can be
; played again without reloading.
; Needs SETSIZE ($F2), RUNMC ($F1), PRINTSTR ($C1), GETSTR ($C2): V0061.28 on.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/adventure_verify.py, V0061.34 image): walkthrough (24 moves) escapes; PLAY AGAIN resets the world and escapes again; 22 parser cases, 22 rule cases, death by vacuum and by air - all as expected (sim, 2026-09-26).
;
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-09-26 - Craig: "It works!"
;
; 645 STELLAR commands, $4000-$4824 (2085 bytes).
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START                              Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 F2 03          SETSIZE 3                          Take $4000-$6FFF: VM1 plus the two blocks above it
; D 4003 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: the index for flags
; D 4007 11 0E 2F 40    LOADXI R14 2F40
; D 400B 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 400E 2F 0E 00 00    WRITEIDX R14 0000                  no line yet
; D 4012 11 04 00 25    LOADXI R4 0025                     TITLE
; D 4016 BD 07 2A       CALL SAY
; NEWGAME:
; D 4019 11 0D 10 60    LOADXI R13 1060
; D 401D 11 0E 2F 20    LOADXI R14 2F20
; D 4021 3B DE 20       COPYMXMY RD RE 20                  STATE := INIT (places + flags)
; D 4024 11 01 00 01    LOADXI R1 0001                     the crew quarters
; D 4028 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000                     no moves yet
; D 402C 11 07 00 FA    LOADXI R7 00FA                     air
; D 4030 11 04 00 26    LOADXI R4 0026                     INTRO
; D 4034 BD 07 2A       CALL SAY
; D 4037 BD 07 38       CALL DESCRIBE
; LOOP:
; D 403A 11 04 00 27    LOADXI R4 0027                     PROMPT
; D 403E BD 07 2A       CALL SAY
; D 4041 11 0C 2F 40    LOADXI R12 2F40
; D 4045 11 0D 2F 40    LOADXI R13 2F40
; D 4049 C2 CD          GETSTR R12 R13                     Read the line (echoed; backspace works)
; D 404B 11 04 00 28    LOADXI R4 0028                     CRLF
; D 404F BD 07 2A       CALL SAY
; D 4052 F1 4C 00       RUNMC 4C00                         Parse: VERB, NOUN, BAD, WBUF
; D 4055 2E 0B 2F 02    READIDX R11 2F02
; D 4059 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 405C A1 00 89       IFFALSEI BADWORD
; D 405F 2E 0B 2F 00    READIDX R11 2F00
; D 4063 21 02          COPYAX Acc -> R2                   R2 = the verb
; D 4065 2E 0B 2F 01    READIDX R11 2F01
; D 4069 21 03          COPYAX Acc -> R3                   R3 = the noun
; D 406B 8C 02          TESTXZ R2
